</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Sx4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Experiments</h2>

<section id="Sx4.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="Sx4.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.SSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Models</span>
We evaluate a diverse set of 20 models on MedFact, comprising 8 open-source and 12 proprietary models:</p>
<ul id="Sx4.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Open-source:</span> II-Medical-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Internet 2025</a>)</cite>, HuatuoGPT-o1-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. 2024</a>)</cite>, DeepSeek-R1 (2025-05-28), DeepSeek-V3 (2025-03-24) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI 2025b</a>)</cite>, Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team 2024</a>)</cite>, Qwen3-235B-A22B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team 2025</a>)</cite>, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-70B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI 2025a</a>)</cite>, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI 2025a</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proprietary:</span> XiaoYi (2025-06-24) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Healthcare 2025</a>)</cite>, GPT-4o (2024-11-20), GPT-4.5, o1, o3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI 2025b</a>)</cite>, Claude 3.7 Sonnet, Gemini 2.5 Flash <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepMind 2025</a>)</cite>, Gemini 2.5 Pro, Grok-4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">xAI 2025</a>)</cite>, Qwen2.5-Max <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team 2024</a>)</cite>, ERNIE-X1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Baidu 2025</a>)</cite>, Doubao-Seed-1.6 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">ByteDance 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Sx4.SSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Among these models, XiaoYi, HuatuoGPT-o1-7B, and II-Medical-8B are specifically trained for the medical domain.
We evaluate Doubao-Seed-1.6 in its standard version and thinking mode, listed as Doubao-Seed-1.6-thinking.
We also establish a human expert baseline, calculated as the average performance of three medical professionals.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx4.SSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.SSx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation Strategies</span>
We evaluate all models using zero-shot and Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al. 2022</a>)</cite> in our main experiments.
We also assess a subset of top-performing models using four advanced reasoning strategies, including recently proposed agent-based frameworks, which might be well-suited for fact-checking:</p>
<ul id="Sx4.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx4.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx4.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MedPrompt</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nori et al. 2023</a>)</cite>: A composite strategy that combines self-generated CoT, retrieval-augmented few-shot examples, and self-consistency <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. 2023b</a>)</cite> for single-model inference.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx4.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx4.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lewis et al. 2020</a>)</cite>: A technique that grounds model outputs by first retrieving relevant documents from an external knowledge corpus to use as context in the prompt.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx4.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx4.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MAD</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liang et al. 2024</a>)</cite>: A multi-agent framework where agents engage in a multi-round debate to reach a consensus, thereby improving the final answer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx4.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx4.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MDAgents</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. 2024</a>)</cite>: A dynamic medical framework that adaptively engages multi-agent collaboration based on the perceived difficulty of the input.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Sx4.SSx1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.SSx1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation Metrics</span>
We evaluate performance on two distinct tasks using Precision, Recall, and F1 score. The full implementation details are in the Appendix.</p>
<ul id="Sx4.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx4.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx4.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Veracity Classification (VC):</span> This binary classification task evaluates a model’s ability to identify a medical text as either correct or incorrect. The “incorrect” label serves as the positive class in calculating metrics.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx4.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx4.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error Localization (EL):</span> For texts correctly classified as incorrect, this task evaluates the model’s ability to identify the span of text containing the error precisely. A prediction is considered a true positive only if the model localizes the correct error span.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Sx4.SSx1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We employ GPT-4o as the automated judge for the EL task. Its reliability is confirmed by strong agreement with human experts (Cohen’s Kappa = 0.87) on a random 10% data sample, validating its use as a proxy for human evaluation.</p>
</div>
