<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Ethics Statement</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Human Annotation and Compensation</span> All expert annotators who contributed to MedFact received fair compensation for their time and expertise at rates that meet or exceed the minimum wage in their respective regions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Privacy and Consent</span> We employed a rigorous anonymization process to remove all Personally Identifiable Information (PII) and ensure privacy protection. Our use of this data is strictly for non-commercial research purposes and complies with the terms of service of source platforms under fair use principles.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Risk of Misinformation</span> The factually incorrect instances in MedFact could be exploited to train models that generate harmful content or to disseminate misinformation directly. We will distribute the dataset under a restrictive license that explicitly prohibits use in clinical or patient-facing applications. The dataset will be accompanied by comprehensive documentation that clearly warns users about the presence of factual errors and specifies that its intended purpose is exclusively for research and benchmarking applications.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bias and Representativeness</span> MedFact focuses exclusively on Chinese medical texts. Consequently, the data, error distributions, and model findings may not generalize to other languages, cultures, or healthcare systems. We caution researchers against drawing overly broad conclusions from our findings and encourage the development of analogous benchmarks for other languages and cultural contexts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Dataset Construction &amp; Statistics</h2>

<section id="A2.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Multi-criteria Filtering</h3>

<div id="A2.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Across the three filtering rounds, the acceptance rates (ratio of passed instances to candidate pool size) were 67.69%, 37.00%, and 23.62%, respectively. The consistency between the model suite’s judgment and medical professionals increased progressively: 69.72%, 84.37%, and 96.40%, respectively, while the reference database size grew from 412 to 624 instances.
Figure <a href="#A6.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix F Limitations &amp; Future Work ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> presents one accepted example, and Figure <a href="#A6.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Appendix F Limitations &amp; Future Work ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> presents three rejected examples from the reference database during the multi-criteria filtering process, illustrating the filtering criteria: overly simplistic, esoteric, and malformed content.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Error Taxonomy Definitions</h3>

<div id="A2.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define eight fine-grained error types in MedFact, organized into two primary categories: <span id="A2.SSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Medical Errors</span> and <span id="A2.SSx2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Non-Medical Errors</span>. The definitions for each subcategory are detailed below.</p>
</div>
