</section>
<section id="A2.SSx4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Data Statistics</h3>

<div id="A2.SSx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tables <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Writing Style Taxonomy Definitions ‣ Appendix B Dataset Construction &amp; Statistics ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Writing Style Taxonomy Definitions ‣ Appendix B Dataset Construction &amp; Statistics ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> present the data distribution across different error types and difficulty levels, respectively. Difficulty levels are determined based on model performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SSx5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Data Examples</h3>

<div id="A2.SSx5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SSx5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A6.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ Appendix F Limitations &amp; Future Work ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> to <a href="#A6.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ Appendix F Limitations &amp; Future Work ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> present examples for each medical error. Figures <a href="#A6.F18" title="Figure 18 ‣ Appendix F Limitations &amp; Future Work ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> to <a href="#A6.F21" title="Figure 21 ‣ Appendix F Limitations &amp; Future Work ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> present examples for each non-medical error.
Figures <a href="#A6.F22" title="Figure 22 ‣ Appendix F Limitations &amp; Future Work ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> to <a href="#A6.F25" title="Figure 25 ‣ Appendix F Limitations &amp; Future Work ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> present examples for each writing style.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A3.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Prompt Templates</h3>

<div id="A3.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A6.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ Appendix F Limitations &amp; Future Work ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> to <a href="#A6.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ Appendix F Limitations &amp; Future Work ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> present the prompts used for zero-shot and CoT prompting. All prompts were originally formulated in Chinese; we provide their corresponding English translations for clarity and reference.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Model Versions</h3>

<div id="A3.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We accessed proprietary models through API calls and deployed open-source models locally.
Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Error Taxonomy Definitions ‣ Appendix B Dataset Construction &amp; Statistics ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> lists the model versions and full names used in our experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">LLM-as-a-Judge</h3>

<div id="A3.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the evaluation of error localization tasks, we assessed the consistency agreement between different models and human experts. DeepSeek-R1, GPT-4o, o1, Claude 3.7 Sonnet, and Gemini 2.5 Pro achieved Cohen’s Kappa values of 0.800, 0.870, 0.870, 0.845, and 0.865, respectively, on a random 10% sample of the veracity classification task results from Doubao-Seed-1.6-thinking, XiaoYi, and Qwen-Max. Considering API costs and the evaluation performance, we selected GPT-4o for the LLM-as-a-judge evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Complete Experimental Results</h2>

<section id="A4.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Full Result Tables</h3>

<div id="A4.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present the complete results of our main experiments in Tables <a href="#A4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Full Result Tables ‣ Appendix D Complete Experimental Results ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and <a href="#A4.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Full Result Tables ‣ Appendix D Complete Experimental Results ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and Figures <a href="#A4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Full Result Tables ‣ Appendix D Complete Experimental Results ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Full Result Tables ‣ Appendix D Complete Experimental Results ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. The results from experiments using advanced evaluation strategies and inference-time scaling are provided in Tables <a href="#A4.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Full Result Tables ‣ Appendix D Complete Experimental Results ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and <a href="#A4.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Full Result Tables ‣ Appendix D Complete Experimental Results ‣ MedFact: Benchmarking the Fact-Checking Capabilities of Large Language Models on Chinese Medical Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, respectively.</p>
</div>
